{% doc %}
  "כתובת למשלוח" in the cart, above the checkout button (drawer and page): the city, the street and the house number
  against Israel Post's lists, before the shopper pays. Shipper and Israel Post refuse a label when the street is not
  spelled as on the list ("הגפן" for "גפן"), the house number is missing, the city is another form of the name ("תל
  אביב", "Haifa") or the parts sit in the wrong fields (only "7" in the street). On a non Plus plan the checkout
  itself cannot be checked or blocked (Shopify Functions in a custom app and checkout UI extensions on the
  information step are Plus only), so the check happens here, and the checked address is set on the cart: Shopify
  fills it in at checkout (Storefront API cartDeliveryAddressesReplace, tokenless; measured on the national store,
  20/11/2026).

  Theme settings › עגלה › "כתובת למשלוח בעגלה" (address_check_mode):
  - off: nothing is rendered.
  - optional (default): the box is there (open on the cart page, folded in the drawer); empty, checkout goes on as
    before; filled, it is checked first, and an address that does not pass stops the press with the reason (with
    "להמשיך לתשלום בלי הבדיקה" as the way out).
  - required: the box is open and must be filled; the product page's quick buy goes through the drawer
    (layout/theme.liquid window.theme.cartConsent, snippets/buy-buttons).
  The order carries the cart attribute "_address_check": "checked", or "kept_as_typed" when a name not on the list was
  kept (the leading _ hides it in checkout; the admin and the dashboard see it), to count how many orders the check saw.
  A street or a city that is not on the list can still be kept as typed ("הכתובת נכונה, להשאיר כפי שכתבתי"): the
  lists can lag behind a new street, and the dashboard checks again before the label.

  The lists are assets (assets/il-localities.json, assets/il-streets-NN.json, from .github/address-check/generate.mjs)
  loaded when the shopper first types; the matching is assets/address-match.js (the dashboard's steps), the element
  assets/address-check.js. No field has a name: nothing here is posted with the cart form, and Enter never submits
  it. Needs JavaScript (.js-only); without it the cart works as before.

  @param {string} [context] - 'drawer' (default) or 'page': the ids (stable, so focus survives the re-render).
  @param {string} [form] - id of the cart form, when the box sits outside it (the cart page's summary).
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes on the element. In the drawer ('cart-drawer__address') the box sits after the
    coupon field, outside the sticky totals, for the same reason: folded or open, it never covers the lines on a phone.

  @example
  {% render 'address-check', context: 'page', form: cart_form_id %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign ac_mode = settings.address_check_mode | default: 'optional'
-%}
{%- if ac_mode != 'off' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign ac_id = 'CartDrawer-Address'
    if context == 'page'
      assign ac_id = 'CartPage-Address'
    endif
    assign ac_open = false
    if context == 'page' or ac_mode == 'required'
      assign ac_open = true
    endif
    capture ac_shards
      for i in (0..11)
        assign ac_n = i | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2
        assign ac_file = 'il-streets-' | append: ac_n | append: '.json'
        echo ac_file | asset_url | json
        unless forloop.last
          echo ','
        endunless
      endfor
    endcapture
  -%}
  <script type="module" src="{{ 'address-check.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  <address-check
    class="address-check js-only{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
    id="{{ ac_id }}"
    data-mode="{{ ac_mode | escape }}"
    {% if form != blank %}data-form="{{ form | escape }}"{% endif %}
    data-localities="{{ 'il-localities.json' | asset_url }}"
  >
    <script type="application/json" data-address-shards>[{{ ac_shards }}]</script>
    <script type="application/json" data-address-strings>
      {
        "load_error": {{ 'cart.address_check.load_error' | t | json }},
        "city_fixed": {{ 'cart.address_check.city_fixed' | t: name: '%name%' | json }},
        "city_maybe": {{ 'cart.address_check.city_maybe' | t: name: '%name%' | json }},
        "city_unknown": {{ 'cart.address_check.city_unknown' | t | json }},
        "city_first": {{ 'cart.address_check.city_first' | t | json }},
        "street_fixed": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_fixed' | t: name: '%name%' | json }},
        "street_maybe": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_maybe' | t: name: '%name%' | json }},
        "street_unknown": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_unknown' | t: city: '%city%' | json }},
        "street_only_number": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_only_number' | t | json }},
        "street_required": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_required' | t | json }},
        "street": {{ 'cart.address_check.street' | t | json }},
        "street_none": {{ 'cart.address_check.street_none' | t | json }},
        "number_required": {{ 'cart.address_check.number_required' | t | json }},
        "number_invalid": {{ 'cart.address_check.number_invalid' | t | json }},
        "keep_typed": {{ 'cart.address_check.keep_typed' | t | json }},
        "yes": {{ 'cart.address_check.yes' | t | json }},
        "ok": {{ 'cart.address_check.ok' | t | json }},
        "required": {{ 'cart.address_check.required' | t | json }},
        "fix_first": {{ 'cart.address_check.fix_first' | t | json }}
      }
    </script>
    <details class="address-check__box"{% if ac_open %} open{% endif %} data-address-details>
      <summary class="address-check__summary">
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'location', size: 18 -%}
        <span class="address-check__title">{{ 'cart.address_check.title' | t }}</span>
        {%- if ac_mode == 'optional' -%}
          <span class="address-check__badge">{{ 'cart.address_check.optional' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-down', size: 16, class: 'address-check__chevron' -%}
      </summary>
      <div class="address-check__body">
        <p class="address-check__intro">{{ 'cart.address_check.intro' | t }}</p>
        <div class="address-check__grid">
          {%- for ac_field in (1..4) -%}
            {%- liquid
              case ac_field
                when 1
                  assign ac_key = 'city'
                  assign ac_label = 'cart.address_check.city' | t
                  assign ac_combo = true
                  assign ac_auto = 'address-level2'
                when 2
                  assign ac_key = 'street'
                  assign ac_label = 'cart.address_check.street' | t
                  assign ac_combo = true
                  assign ac_auto = 'off'
                when 3
                  assign ac_key = 'number'
                  assign ac_label = 'cart.address_check.number' | t
                  assign ac_combo = false
                  assign ac_auto = 'off'
                else
                  assign ac_key = 'extra'
                  assign ac_label = 'cart.address_check.extra' | t
                  assign ac_combo = false
                  assign ac_auto = 'address-line2'
              endcase
              assign ac_input = ac_id | append: '-' | append: ac_key
            -%}
            <div class="address-check__field address-check__field--{{ ac_key }}" data-field="{{ ac_key }}">
              <label class="address-check__label" for="{{ ac_input }}" data-label>{{ ac_label }}</label>
              <input
                class="input address-check__input"
                type="text"
                id="{{ ac_input }}"
                dir="auto"
                autocomplete="{% if ac_combo %}off{% else %}{{ ac_auto }}{% endif %}"
                spellcheck="false"
                {% if ac_key == 'number' %}inputmode="text" maxlength="6"{% endif %}
                {% if ac_combo %}
                  role="combobox"
                  aria-autocomplete="list"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="{{ ac_input }}-List"
                {% endif %}
                aria-describedby="{{ ac_input }}-Message"
                data-input="{{ ac_key }}"
              >
              {%- if ac_combo -%}
                <ul class="address-check__list" id="{{ ac_input }}-List" role="listbox" aria-label="{{ ac_label }}" hidden data-list></ul>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="address-check__message form-message" id="{{ ac_input }}-Message" data-message></div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        <p class="address-check__status form-message" role="status" data-status></p>
        {%- if ac_mode == 'optional' -%}
          <button class="link address-check__skip" type="button" hidden data-skip>{{ 'cart.address_check.skip' | t }}</button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </details>
  </address-check>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .address-check {
    display: block;
  }

  /* In the drawer: scrolls with the lines, pushed down to the totals (as the coupon field, which it follows). */
  .cart-drawer__address {
    margin: auto var(--space-md) 0;
    padding-block-end: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .cart-drawer__discount + .cart-drawer__address,
  .cart-drawer__address + .cart-drawer__footer {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  /* A field (and its list) scrolled to is kept clear of the sticky totals under it (assets/address-check.js). */
  .cart-drawer__address .address-check__field,
  .cart-drawer__address .address-check__list {
    scroll-margin-block: var(--space-sm) 16rem;
  }

  .address-check__box {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
  }

  .address-check__summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .address-check__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .address-check__badge {
    padding: 0.125rem var(--space-xs);
    border-radius: var(--radius-badge);
    background-color: var(--color-hover-bg);
    color: var(--color-brand);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .address-check__chevron {
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .address-check__box[open] .address-check__chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .address-check__body {
    padding: 0 var(--space-sm) var(--space-sm);
  }

  .address-check__intro {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  /* One column: the messages under a field (with their buttons) get the full width. */
  .address-check__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .address-check__field {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .address-check__field--number .address-check__input {
    max-width: 9rem;
  }

  .address-check__label {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .address-check__input {
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .address-check__input[aria-invalid="true"] {
    border-color: var(--color-error);
  }

  /* In the flow, under its field, not over the page: in the drawer the sticky totals would cover a floating list,
     and on the cart page it would cover the checkout button. */
  .address-check__list {
    max-height: 15rem;
    margin: 0.125rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.25rem 0;
    overflow-y: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-control);
    border-radius: var(--radius-input);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    box-shadow: 0 0.5rem 1.5rem rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .address-check__option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .address-check__option[aria-selected="true"],
  .address-check__option:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-hover-bg);
  }

  /* The text wraps, and the buttons ("כן, גפן", "להשאיר כפי שכתבתי") follow it on their own lines. */
  .address-check__message {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-xs);
  }

  .address-check__message > span {
    flex: 1 0 100%;
  }

  .address-check__message:not(:empty),
  .address-check__status:not(:empty) {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .address-check__message[data-tone="error"],
  .address-check__status[data-tone="error"] {
    color: var(--color-error);
  }

  .address-check__message[data-tone="ok"],
  .address-check__status[data-tone="ok"] {
    color: var(--color-brand);
  }

  .address-check__choice {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-xs);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-control);
    border-radius: var(--radius-badge);
    background: none;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .address-check__skip {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
